commit 7318b8e91bab41fff4c8ac0060b030512a1ca67e
Author: Marcus Schack Abildskov <work@marcus-sa.dev>
Date:   Fri Nov 20 11:50:12 2026 +0100

    feat(node-local-persistent-volume): volume-pool guest provisioning and second-disk launch
    
    The production Vmm now renders VmConfig.volume as the second --disk
    (DiskAttachment::volume: direct=on, serial=ovd-volume). Guest-kit
    preparation builds a sparse backing disk template holding a GPT
    partition labelled overdrive-volumes with the PV and the overdrive VG
    (4 MiB extents); each volume-pool guest boots a fresh copy as its second
    disk, with the LVM toolchain, sfdisk, flock, dmsetup and the dm-flakey
    module staged. The Tier-3 volume tests run in that guest and are proven
    RED on their own markers.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Step-Id: 01-01
    Task-Id: node-local-persistent-volume

